# Optional process environment settings for the local service.
# PowerShell example: $env:BRIDGE_PORT = '4173'; npm start
# BRIDGE_PORT=4173
# BRIDGE_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\<you>\ContextBridgeData
# On Windows keep the data folder inside your user profile: files there inherit its permissions.
# The service does not automatically load .env files. Set variables in the shell,
# or use: node --env-file=.env server/index.ts
# Keep BRIDGE_DATA_DIR private; it contains Codex credentials, a saved Anthropic API key, files and backups.
# Never add API secrets to VITE_* variables; those are exposed in the browser.

# AI provider used until someone chooses one in the workbench: codex (default) or claude.
# BRIDGE_PROVIDER=claude
# Anthropic API key for Claude Code. A key saved in the workbench takes precedence.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Personal use on your own computer only: allow Claude Code to use the account already
# signed in to the claude command. Do not enable for anything offered to other people.
# BRIDGE_CLAUDE_LOCAL_LOGIN=1
